                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "U8qWsI",
                  "x": 150,
                  "y": 104,
                  "name": "Page",
                  "width": 540,
                  "height": 640,
                  "fill": "#0B0B0B",
                  "stroke": "#1C1C1C",
                  "strokeWidth": 1,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 18,
                  "padding": [
                    48,
                    52
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Nc02u",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#3A3A3A",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "7.1   An Introduction to Discrete Probability",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 20,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Ytnyd",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#3A3A3A",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Probability began with games of chance. To talk about it precisely we need a few words. An experiment is a procedure that yields one of a given set of possible outcomes.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "n4f7kw",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#F2F2F2",
                      "effect": {
                        "type": "shadow",
                        "shadowType": "outer",
                        "color": "#FFFFFF40",
                        "blur": 18
                      },
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The sample space S of an experiment is the set of all possible outcomes. An event E is a subset of the sample space.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "B9yW7B",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#4A4A4A",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "If S is a finite, nonempty sample space of equally likely outcomes, and E is an event, the probability of E is  p(E) = |E| / |S|.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Ny9fx",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#262626",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Example 1.  An urn holds four blue balls and five red balls. What is the probability that a ball chosen at random is blue?",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "o6OKF",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#1C1C1C",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Solution.  There are nine possible outcomes, and four of them give a blue ball, so the probability is 4/9.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 15,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
