    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "W5wRST",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 24789,
      "name": "9c · Where it looked: round 3",
      "fill": "#000000",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 28,
      "padding": 48,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Wf8kI",
          "name": "Board title",
          "fill": "#E6E6E6",
          "content": "9c · Where it looked: round 3",
          "fontFamily": "Source Sans 3",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "siSmw",
          "name": "Board note",
          "fill": "#8D8D8D",
          "content": "Three ways to push C. Same moment: Claude Code read page 1 closely, skimmed page 2, jumped to page 3 and is on Theorem 1 now.",
          "fontFamily": "Source Sans 3",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "p6Tmj",
          "name": "Variants",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 32,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "V1gla",
              "name": "C1 · Reading trail",
              "clip": true,
              "width": 1200,
              "height": 680,
              "fill": "#000000",
              "stroke": "#161616",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "layout": "none",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "GNXHE",
                  "x": 32,
                  "y": 28,
                  "name": "Tag",
                  "fill": "#E6E6E6",
                  "content": "C1 · Reading trail",
                  "fontFamily": "Source Sans 3",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "QKdAj",
                  "x": 32,
                  "y": 54,
                  "name": "Tag note",
                  "fill": "#8D8D8D",
                  "content": "The pages it opened, side by side. Ink shows only where it read. A thin trail joins the spots in the order it read them, and ends in Halley's comet.",
                  "fontFamily": "Source Sans 3",
                  "fontSize": 13.5,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "boADn",
                  "x": 40,
                  "y": 120,
                  "name": "Page 1",
                  "clip": true,
                  "width": 340,
                  "height": 360,
                  "fill": "#090909",
                  "stroke": "#1A1A1A",
                  "strokeWidth": 1,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 12,
                  "padding": 26,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "OxnPd",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#5A5A5A",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "7.1  An Introduction to Discrete Probability",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "qJOft",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#1C1C1C",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Probability theory dates back to the seventeenth century, when gamblers asked mathematicians to settle questions about games of chance.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "PG2CX",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#D9D9D9",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "An experiment is a procedure that yields one of a given set of possible outcomes.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "wI0Jk",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#D9D9D9",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The sample space of the experiment is the set of possible outcomes. An event is a subset of the sample space.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "nOdDK",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#D9D9D9",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Definition 1. If S is a finite nonempty sample space of equally likely outcomes, and E is an event, then the probability of E is p(E) = |E| / |S|.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "S8uPX",
                  "x": 40,
                  "y": 490,
                  "name": "Page no",
                  "fill": "#4A4A4A",
                  "content": "page 1",
                  "fontFamily": "JetBrains Mono",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "DPTWH",
                  "x": 420,
                  "y": 120,
                  "name": "Page 2",
                  "clip": true,
                  "width": 340,
                  "height": 360,
                  "fill": "#090909",
                  "stroke": "#1A1A1A",
                  "strokeWidth": 1,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 12,
                  "padding": 26,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Ixxkd",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#5A5A5A",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Example 1. An urn contains four blue balls and five red balls. What is the probability that a ball chosen at random is blue?",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "qzPzq",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#1C1C1C",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Solution. There are nine possible outcomes, and four of these produce a blue ball. Hence the probability is 4/9.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "uZCiY",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#1C1C1C",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Example 2. What is the probability that when two dice are rolled, the sum of the numbers is seven?",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "n3af5",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#1C1C1C",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Solution. There are 36 equally likely outcomes. Six of them sum to seven, so the probability is 6/36 = 1/6.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "liogK",
                  "x": 420,
                  "y": 490,
                  "name": "Page no",
                  "fill": "#4A4A4A",
                  "content": "page 2",
                  "fontFamily": "JetBrains Mono",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "V4Mcs",
                  "x": 800,
                  "y": 120,
                  "name": "Page 3",
                  "clip": true,
                  "width": 340,
                  "height": 360,
                  "fill": "#090909",
                  "stroke": "#1A1A1A",
                  "strokeWidth": 1,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 12,
                  "padding": 26,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "q1c5t0",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#D9D9D9",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Complements and Unions of Events",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "SPqz5",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#FFFFFF",
                      "effect": {
                        "type": "shadow",
                        "shadowType": "outer",
                        "color": "#FFFFFF66",
                        "blur": 14
                      },
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Theorem 1. Let E be an event in a sample space S. The probability of the complement of E is p(Ē) = 1 − p(E).",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "sP9dM",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#5A5A5A",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Proof. Note that |Ē| = |S| − |E|. Hence p(Ē) = (|S| − |E|) / |S| = 1 − p(E).",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "OkzPA",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#1C1C1C",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Example 10. A sequence of 10 bits is chosen at random. What is the probability that at least one of these bits is 0?",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 12.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
