                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "iLlR8",
                  "x": 32,
                  "y": 54,
                  "name": "Tag note",
                  "fill": "#8D8D8D",
                  "content": "The whole file as one dark scroll. Text only lights up where the agent's eyes have been. Arcs in the margin show every jump, and why it jumped.",
                  "fontFamily": "Source Sans 3",
                  "fontSize": 13.5,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "I6iM8",
                  "x": 60,
                  "y": 110,
                  "name": "Scroll",
                  "width": 520,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 14,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "YpGtS",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#4A4A4A",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "7.1  An Introduction to Discrete Probability",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 16,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "l9GKDs",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#141414",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Probability theory dates back to the seventeenth century, when gamblers asked mathematicians to settle questions about games of chance.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "L0Nwe",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#E6E6E6",
                      "effect": {
                        "type": "shadow",
                        "shadowType": "outer",
                        "color": "#FFFFFF26",
                        "blur": 10
                      },
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "An experiment is a procedure that yields one of a given set of possible outcomes.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "u8o5W",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#E6E6E6",
                      "effect": {
                        "type": "shadow",
                        "shadowType": "outer",
                        "color": "#FFFFFF26",
                        "blur": 10
                      },
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The sample space of the experiment is the set of possible outcomes. An event is a subset of the sample space.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "gcmme",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#E6E6E6",
                      "effect": {
                        "type": "shadow",
                        "shadowType": "outer",
                        "color": "#FFFFFF26",
                        "blur": 10
                      },
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Definition 1. If S is a finite nonempty sample space of equally likely outcomes, and E is an event, then the probability of E is p(E) = |E| / |S|.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "dcr5w",
                      "name": "Page break",
                      "fill": "#2F2F2F",
                      "content": "page 2",
                      "fontFamily": "JetBrains Mono",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "JzgKZ",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#4A4A4A",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Example 1. An urn contains four blue balls and five red balls. What is the probability that a ball chosen at random is blue?",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "ZqKZo",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#141414",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Solution. There are nine possible outcomes, and four of these produce a blue ball. Hence the probability is 4/9.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "jXcHh",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#141414",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Example 2. What is the probability that when two dice are rolled, the sum of the numbers is seven?",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "EkzZr",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#141414",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Solution. There are 36 equally likely outcomes. Six of them sum to seven, so the probability is 6/36 = 1/6.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "xl1df",
                      "name": "Page break",
                      "fill": "#2F2F2F",
                      "content": "page 3",
                      "fontFamily": "JetBrains Mono",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "dJekR",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#E6E6E6",
                      "effect": {
                        "type": "shadow",
                        "shadowType": "outer",
                        "color": "#FFFFFF26",
                        "blur": 10
                      },
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Complements and Unions of Events",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 16,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "ZbD0g",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#FFFFFF",
                      "effect": {
                        "type": "shadow",
                        "shadowType": "outer",
                        "color": "#FFFFFF80",
                        "blur": 16
                      },
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Theorem 1. Let E be an event in a sample space S. The probability of the complement of E is p(Ē) = 1 − p(E).",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Vk0ul",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#4A4A4A",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Proof. Note that |Ē| = |S| − |E|. Hence p(Ē) = (|S| − |E|) / |S| = 1 − p(E).",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "O2SJPs",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#141414",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Example 10. A sequence of 10 bits is chosen at random. What is the probability that at least one of these bits is 0?",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "T3gap",
                      "name": "Para",
                      "fill": "#141414",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Theorem 2. Let E1 and E2 be events in S. Then p(E1 ∪ E2) = p(E1) + p(E2) − p(E1 ∩ E2).",
                      "lineHeight": 1.55,
                      "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "rectangle",
                  "id": "eGQQt",
                  "x": 40,
                  "y": 900,
                  "name": "Fade",
                  "fill": {
                    "type": "gradient",
