              "layout": "none",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "EAPrD",
                  "x": 110,
                  "y": -119,
                  "name": "Pages (scrolling)",
                  "rotation": -1.2,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 28,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "d0vd71",
                      "name": "Page 2",
                      "width": 460,
                      "fill": "#E9E9E7",
                      "effect": {
                        "type": "shadow",
                        "shadowType": "outer",
                        "color": "#000000CC",
                        "offset": {
                          "x": 0,
                          "y": 24
                        },
                        "blur": 48
                      },
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 12,
                      "padding": [
                        40,
                        44
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "f9ohx",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Example 1. An urn contains four blue balls and five red balls. What is the probability that a ball chosen at random is blue?",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 12.5,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "Mdwcu",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Solution. There are nine possible outcomes, and four of these produce a blue ball. Hence the probability is 4/9.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 12.5,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "POtuj",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Example 2. What is the probability that when two dice are rolled, the sum of the numbers is seven?",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 12.5,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "mp9aw",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Solution. There are 36 equally likely outcomes. Six of them sum to seven, so the probability is 6/36 = 1/6.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 12.5,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "hidZz",
                          "name": "Folio",
                          "fill": "#8A8A8A",
                          "content": "2",
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 11,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "vchDA",
                      "name": "Page 3",
                      "width": 460,
                      "fill": "#E9E9E7",
                      "effect": {
                        "type": "shadow",
                        "shadowType": "outer",
                        "color": "#000000CC",
                        "offset": {
                          "x": 0,
                          "y": 24
                        },
                        "blur": 48
                      },
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 12,
                      "padding": [
                        40,
                        44
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "ZcIzr",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Complements and Unions of Events",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 15,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "K6dMzB",
                          "name": "Reading here",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "fill": "#00000012",
                          "stroke": "#1A1A1A",
                          "strokeWidth": {
                            "left": 2
                          },
                          "layout": "vertical",
                          "padding": [
                            6,
                            8
                          ],
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "jqIyq",
                              "name": "Para",
                              "fill": "#111111",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Theorem 1. Let E be an event in a sample space S. The probability of the complement of E is p(Ē) = 1 − p(E).",
                              "lineHeight": 1.5,
                              "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                              "fontSize": 12.5,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "UZo6x",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Proof. Note that |Ē| = |S| − |E|. Hence p(Ē) = (|S| − |E|) / |S| = 1 − p(E).",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 12.5,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "GberO",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Example 10. A sequence of 10 bits is chosen at random. What is the probability that at least one of these bits is 0?",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 12.5,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "y2lyTy",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Theorem 2. Let E1 and E2 be events in S. Then p(E1 ∪ E2) = p(E1) + p(E2) − p(E1 ∩ E2).",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 12.5,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "HKTd5",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Solution. Let E be the event that at least one of the 10 bits is 0. Then Ē is the event that all the bits are 1. Because the sample space S is the set of all bit strings of length 10, p(E) = 1 − p(Ē) = 1 − 1/2¹⁰ = 1023/1024.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 12.5,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "x18MkX",
                          "name": "Folio",
                          "fill": "#8A8A8A",
                          "content": "3",
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 11,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "KsIpd",
                      "name": "Page 4",
                      "width": 460,
                      "fill": "#E9E9E7",
                      "effect": {
                        "type": "shadow",
                        "shadowType": "outer",
                        "color": "#000000CC",
                        "offset": {
                          "x": 0,
                          "y": 24
                        },
                        "blur": 48
                      },
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 12,
                      "padding": [
                        40,
                        44
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "W4NgN1",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Example 11. What is the probability that a positive integer selected at random from the set of positive integers not exceeding 100 is divisible by either 2 or 5?",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 12.5,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "xtpb1",
                          "name": "Para",
                          "fill": "#2B2B2B",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Solution. Let E1 be the event that the integer is divisible by 2, and E2 the event that it is divisible by 5.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 12.5,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "pnDlp",
                          "name": "Folio",
                          "fill": "#8A8A8A",
                          "content": "4",
                          "fontFamily": "STIX Two Text",
                          "fontSize": 11,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
